3,Doutai language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/doutai_language,"Doutai (ISO 639-3: tds; also known as Taori, Taori-So, or Tolitai) is a severely endangered Lakes Plain language of the Trans-New Guinea phylum, spoken by an estimated 250 to 500 people as of 1991 in the remote Toli-Dou village of the Lakes Plain region in Papua, Indonesia.",Doutai,Lakes Plain
